@tradition scone-morning
// Round 1 (CS1's pitch, the user's yes): on his rest day Emeka Halloran bakes one batch of scones, Brennan inspects them, the Works tea corner gets them warm. Every 6 weeks from week 10 (Days 70, 112...).
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
k: 1300
title: Scone morning
when: every 6 weeks sunday week 4 from day 64
at: 09:30-10:15
min: 20
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
who: halloran-emeka always, brennan 50%, works 45%, tea-break 35%, everyone 8%
anim: halloran-emeka talk, everyone drink
host: halloran-emeka
from: halloran-emeka
invite: host=halloran-emeka odds=25% line="Scones in the tea corner tomorrow morning. Warm ones. And a joke, free."

== mail
- Scone morning tomorrow, {time}, in the Works tea corner. One batch, Brennan's passed it. One joke per scone. You can't have one without the other.

== ask
- Halloran's baked. Tea corner, now, before Works eats the lot.
- Scone morning! He's got the tin out. The one with the dent.
- Going for a scone? Brace yourself for the joke.   #funny

== here
- Butter's there. Jam's there. Joke's coming.   #funny
- Still warm. Mind your fingers.
- This batch got a nod from Brennan. A nod!
- Lovely. Have another. Go on.   #warm

== thanks
- Halloran hands you a warm scone from the dented tin, and a joke with it. The scone is excellent.   #warm

== chatter
- Halloran's scones were still warm at the tea corner. The joke wasn't.   #funny
- I had two scones. I heard two jokes. Fair trade.   #funny
- The tea corner smelled of baking all morning. Lovely way to start a Sunday.   #warm
